================================================================================
=== COLLISION (binding finding — resolved, fully transparent per Covenant 7/9) ===
================================================================================
The prompt's native filename `ConfirmDialog.*` is ALREADY OWNED by sibling prompt 0012, which shipped
the GENERIC destructive-action dialog `web/src/components/ui/ConfirmDialog.tsx` to the same path. Those
10 files are committed and define public Swift symbols `ConfirmDialog` / `ConfirmDialogModel` /
`ConfirmDialogProjection` / … and diagnostics slug "ConfirmDialog" (verified: 0012's
ConfirmDialog.Adapter.swift L33 `slug = "ConfirmDialog"`; 0012 log header `web source:
web/src/components/ui/ConfirmDialog.tsx`).

THIS prompt (0001) targets a DIFFERENT web component — `web/src/components/ai/ConfirmDialog.tsx`,
exported `AiConfirmDialog`: the AI tool-use approval dialog (tool name + JSON args + mutating/read
intro). Both web components exist and are distinct, live surfaces (confirmed: both files present).

Writing `ConfirmDialog.*` would (a) OVERWRITE a committed sibling surface (Covenant 7 "no predecessor
bypass") and (b) define DUPLICATE Swift symbols inside module TeslaSync -> hard compile error.

RESOLUTION: ship the AI dialog under `AiConfirmDialog.*` with distinct `AiConfirm*` symbols, the web
source's own `ai.confirm.*` i18n keys (naturally namespaced, no clash with 0012's `confirm.*`), and
slug "AiConfirmDialog" (so the two surfaces stay separable in diagnostics — Covenant 9 "no silent
drift"). NO 0012 file is touched. This is the faithful realization of the prompt's true intent (ship
the ai/ConfirmDialog surface at parity) without regressing a sibling. The deviations from the prompt's
literal `ConfirmDialog.*` / slug "ConfirmDialog" are documented here rather than hidden.

